# THE BUILD FLOOR, and the reclaim trigger that sits above it. One
# definition, read — never sourced, never retyped — by the two scripts
# that used to spell it separately:
#
#   infra/gate.sh                      refuses a gate (and the --lint /
#                                      --quick pre-flights) below
#                                      GATE_MIN_FREE_GB free on the
#                                      volume it builds on
#   infra/cluster/dev-scratch-reclaim.sh
#                                      reclaims /work once it falls below
#                                      GATE_MIN_FREE_GB + WORK_RECLAIM_MARGIN_GB
#
# WHY ONE FILE (backlog 99ce8744, CLAUDE.md §9a). Measured 2026-09-24
# ~23:00Z: /work had 12 GB free of 40 GB (339 worktrees, 15 GB). The
# gate refused below 12 (`BOSS_GATE_MIN_FREE_GB:-12` in gate.sh) while
# the reclaim acted only below 6 (`BOSS_WORK_FLOOR_GB:-6` in the
# reclaim, and the same 6 in its sidecar's env), so the automatic pass
# that exists to keep /work clear could never fire before a builder's
# pre-flight was refused — and two builders in one hour lowered the
# gate's floor by hand instead. Two numbers under no mechanism had
# drifted into the one order that makes the reclaim useless.
#
# WHY THE MARGIN IS AN ADDEND, NOT A SECOND FLOOR. The reclaim must act
# BEFORE the gate refuses, so its trigger is defined as the gate's floor
# plus a margin and cannot be set below it: raise the gate's floor and
# the reclaim follows. 6 GB is measured, not guessed: 178 worktrees were
# created under /work/boss/.claude/worktrees in the 24 hours to
# 2026-09-24 23:30Z at ~43 MB each (a fresh checkout), ~7.6 GB a day —
# so the margin is most of a day of worktree growth, against an hourly
# pass.
#
# THE /scratch FLOOR (backlog 4cc39798, 2026-10-20) — read by
# infra/cluster/dev-scratch-reclaim.sh (both the hourly pass and the
# build-triggered `--scratch-floor` wt-cargo runs). On a Talos node
# /scratch is the kubelet's nodefs, the disk the estate comparison
# judges `disk_tight` for a cluster node, in
# crates/orchestrators/boss-dispatcher-handlers/src/handlers/estate_compare.rs,
# at the HIGHER of two floors:
#   - 35% of the disk (DISK_TIGHT_FLOOR_PCT), held between 16 GB and
#     200 GB (DISK_TIGHT_FLOOR_GB, DISK_TIGHT_HEADROOM_CEILING_GB) —
#     the one that rules on a disk under ~727 GB;
#   - Longhorn's replica refusal at 25% (LONGHORN_MINIMAL_AVAILABLE_PCT)
#     plus a 10% margin (LONGHORN_FLOOR_MARGIN_PCT), 27.5% — the one
#     that rules on w-1 (929 GB: 256 GB against 200).
# The script's own default was 25 — Longhorn's line exactly — so on w-1
# (813 per-run targets) it logged "251GB free >= 232GB floor (25%) — no
# build-cache reclaim" while disk_tight fired below 256 three readings
# running, and by the time it would act Longhorn was already refusing
# volumes. The reclaim must act BEFORE the alarm at every disk size, so
# its floor has the alarm's shape, each term above the alarm's own:
#   max(SCRATCH_RECLAIM_FLOOR_PCT of the disk,
#       min(SCRATCH_RECLAIM_HEADROOM_PCT of the disk,
#           SCRATCH_RECLAIM_HEADROOM_CEILING_GB))
# 30% is 278 GB on w-1, 22 GB above the alarm (about half an hour of
# the ~40 GB/h builders were measured filling it at, against a pass
# that wt-cargo runs before every build); there the headroom term is
# capped at 220 and does not rule. On a 500 GB disk it does: 200 GB
# against the alarm's 175, where a 30% share alone (150) sat UNDER it
# — and a pin that read only the Longhorn pair passed that (review
# 1eee8160). The order is pinned at every disk size from 100 GB to
# 10 TB (the dev pod requests 150Gi of ephemeral storage, so no smaller
# disk holds /scratch), with each side's rounding and all five of the
# estate's constants read out of its source, by
# the_build_floor_lives_once.rs `the_scratch_reclaim_floor_sits_above_the_estates_disk_tight_floor`:
# raise any of them past these lines and that test names the disk.
#
# A reader parses `NAME=<whole number>` lines; anything else is prose.
GATE_MIN_FREE_GB=12
WORK_RECLAIM_MARGIN_GB=6
SCRATCH_RECLAIM_FLOOR_PCT=30
SCRATCH_RECLAIM_HEADROOM_PCT=40
SCRATCH_RECLAIM_HEADROOM_CEILING_GB=220
